  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-1.55<Z<1.55).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/45d71abed85d91a5a1b150fb741bcc8fa9967f7b2b8d77df35423a909b1e8522.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.55<Z<1.55) & =P(Z<1.55)-P(Z\\le -1.55) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.55)-P(Z\\le -1.55) \\\\  & =\u03a6(1.55)-\u03a6(-1.55)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\u03a6(1.55)=0.9394,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $\u03a6(-1.55).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-1.55) & =P(Z\\le -1.55) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 1.55) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<1.55) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 1.55) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(1.55) \\\\  & =1-0.9394 \\\\  & =0.0606\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.55<Z<1.55) & =\u03a6(1.55)-\u03a6(-1.55) \\\\  & =0.9394-0.0606 \\\\  & =0.8788.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
